 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "Échame una mano",
  "alumno": "Give me a hand"
 },
 "intro": "How to ask a friend, a colleague and a stranger for help, and the many ways of saying yes.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "echar una mano",
   "significado": "to give someone a hand",
   "pron": "e-CHAR U-na MA-no",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is colloquial: «échame una mano». Nothing is really thrown: it is just a way of asking for help.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "alcanzar",
   "significado": "to pass, to hand over",
   "pron": "al-kan-THAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Here it is not «llegar»: «¿me alcanzas la sal?» asks someone to pass you what you cannot reach.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "te agradecería que",
   "significado": "I would be grateful if you…",
   "pron": "te a-gra-de-the-RI-a ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "After «que» comes the imperfect subjunctive: «te agradecería que vinieras». With «usted»: «le agradecería que…».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "rogar",
   "significado": "to beg, to request earnestly",
   "pron": "rro-GAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The o becomes «ue»: «ruego», «ruegas». You say «te ruego que» plus a subjunctive: «te ruego que esperes».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "hace falta que",
   "significado": "it is necessary that",
   "pron": "A-the FAL-ta ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It takes the subjunctive: «hace falta que llegues pronto». With «que», the verb «hace» always stays singular.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me harías un favor",
   "significado": "would you do me a favour?",
   "pron": "me a-RI-as un fa-BOR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The conditional «harías» softens the request. Without it you would say «¿me haces un favor?», more direct.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "solicitar",
   "significado": "to request (formal)",
   "pron": "so-li-thi-TAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It belongs to letters and forms: «solicito una cita». In conversation people say «pedir».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "colaboración",
   "significado": "cooperation, help",
   "pron": "ko-la-bo-ra-THYON",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is feminine and ends in -ción: «la colaboración». It comes from «colaborar», which is to work with others.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "con mucho gusto",
   "significado": "with pleasure",
   "pron": "kon MU-cho GUS-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You use it to accept a request gladly. It sounds warmer than a plain «sí».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cómo no",
   "significado": "of course",
   "pron": "KO-mo no",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It looks like a question, but it is a very polite «sí»: to «¿me ayudas?» you can answer «¡cómo no!».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por supuesto",
   "significado": "of course",
   "pron": "por su-PWES-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is two separate words. It works to accept a request and also to confirm an idea.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "será un placer",
   "significado": "it will be a pleasure",
   "pron": "se-RA un pla-THER",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is very polite and a little formal. «Será» is the future of «ser» and has an accent on the a.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cuando quieras",
   "significado": "whenever you like",
   "pron": "KWAN-do KYE-ras",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You let the other person choose the moment. With «usted» you say «cuando quiera».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "de paso",
   "significado": "while I am at it",
   "pron": "de PA-so",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It adds an extra action while you do another: «voy a correos y, de paso, compro sellos».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "necesitaría",
   "significado": "would need (necesitar)",
   "pron": "ne-the-si-ta-RI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «necesitar», in the conditional: a polite way to ask for something.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "echaras",
   "significado": "would give (a hand) (echar)",
   "pron": "e-CHA-ras",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«echar una mano» means help someone. The subjunctive «echaras» follows «que».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "furgoneta",
   "significado": "van",
   "pron": "fur-go-NE-ta",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Think of «furgón» plus «-eta»: a small van for carrying things.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "garaje",
   "significado": "garage",
   "pron": "ga-RA-he",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The j sounds like h: «garaje» is pronounced ga-RA-he.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "perdones",
   "significado": "forgive (perdonar), subjunctive",
   "pron": "per-DO-nes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «perdonar». Here it means forgiving someone, in the subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "solicito",
   "significado": "I request (solicitar)",
   "pron": "so-LI-thi-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«solicito» is formal language, typical of letters and offices.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
